==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|frm}} {{term|solliciter|lang=frm}}, from {{etyl|la}} {{term|sollicitare|sollicitāre||lang=la}}, present active participle of {{term|sollicito|sollicitō|stir, disturb; look after|lang=la}}, from {{term|sollicitus||literally 'thoroughly moved'; agitated, anxious, punctilious}}, from {{term|sollus||whole, entire|lang=la}} + perfect passive participle of {{term|cieo|cieō|shake, excite, cite, to put in motion|lang=la}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|sə-lĭs'ĭt}}
* {{IPA| /səˈlɪsɪt/}}
* {{audio|en-us-solicit.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|ɪsɪt}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# To persistently [[endeavor]] to obtain an object, or [[bring about]] an event.
# To [[woo]]; to [[court]].
# To persuade or [[incite]] one to commit some act, especially illegal or sexual behavior.
# To offer to perform sexual activity, especially when for a [[payment]].
# To make a [[petition]].
# {{archaic}} To [[disturb]] or trouble; to [[harass]].

